61} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864} :answer-field/id #uuid "a70f3f5c-4515-5830-8325-e90e481a964b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a501a88c-c742-55d1-9428-8cda49f09e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-316649" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-(-5))(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+4x+20) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100.$"}]}
